@startuml review_report_03_own_grid_density
' Review unit 03 of 03 -- see docs/review_report.md for the series.
' State AFTER commit e059ed9 (commits f08d3e9, 15aaa8a, e059ed9).
' Every number below is from a run of the cases at commits 15aaa8a and e059ed9.
' Render: plantuml docs/review_report_03_own_grid_density.puml

title Unit 03 -- density on the own grid; rounding always reported; coverage for var0 only (4998269..e059ed9)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "the call -- unchanged" {
  :cases A/B, single variable and S, as in unit 00
  <b>case O</b>: var_dims=[3, 3], overlap=0.05 (both on every dimension);
}

partition "GenerateData._configure_multi_var" {
  #C8E6C9:1. MultiVarDimensionsConfig first -> var_dims_indices
  var0 on (x0, x1, x2), var1 on (x1, x2);
  #C8E6C9:2. grid_fractions = own grid / full grid per variable
  var0 256 / 256 = 1.0, var1 64 / 256 = 0.25;
  #C8E6C9:3. MultiVarSparsityConfig.setup_from_parameter(..., grid_fractions)
  n_i = rint(d_i / d_max * num_obs * f_i)
  var1: 0.1 / 0.4 * 102 * 0.25 = 6.375 -> <b>6</b>;
  #FFCDD2:before: densities first, n_i = rint(d_i / d_max * num_obs)
  var1: 0.1 / 0.4 * 102 = 25.5 -> 26, i.e. 0.1 of the FULL grid;
  note right
    Dimensions and densities draw from
    independent streams, so swapping the
    two setups moves no draw. f_i = 1 for
    a variable on every dimension: its
    count, and its data, do not change.
  end note
}

partition "place, store -- unchanged code, fewer var1 sites" {
  :case A: var1 6 sites on its 64 cells
  F1 0.4561 -> <b>0.1053</b> (6 of 57 projected reference cells, the most 6 sites reach);
}

partition "GenerationReport" {
  #C8E6C9:from_chunks: density = occupied / prod(shape[d] for d in var_dims_indices[i])
  the own grid, as from_arrays already measured it;
  #C8E6C9:requested_density(gen, i): the density as the caller gave it
  one variable: the constructor's density (validation rewrites
  var_densities to the rounded figure)
  compared at the default tolerance, not 1e-3;
  #C8E6C9:coverage row for <b>var0 only</b>, in both paths
  the LHS stage guarantees it for var0 and for no other variable
  measure_chunk sends var0's axis vectors only;
  #FFCDD2:coverage row for every variable; the chunked path checked
  axes a variable does not have (chunk arrays keep every dimension);
}

#FFF9C4:<b>case A</b>, serial and parallel now agree on density
                      unit 02 serial / parallel     unit 03 both
observations var1     26 / 26                       6
density var1          0.40625 / 0.101562            0.09375
density var0          0.398438 differs              0.398438 differs
overlap F1 var1       0.45614                       0.105263
coverage              var0 yes, var1 yes / x0       var0 yes (no var1 row)
ds.nc 15729 B, var1 holds 6 values;

#FFF9C4:<b>case S</b> (d=0.4 for var1 on 64 cells): 26 sites, density 0.40625,
no saturation; before: 64 sites, density 1.0
<b>single variable</b>: density 0.4 vs 0.398438 now reads differs
(it read match: the requested side was the rounded value);

:<b>case O</b> and every variable on every dimension: byte-identical
to unit 02. <b>single variable</b> data: byte-identical.
Serial equals parallel in every case;

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since unit 02 |

  <b>What to review in unit 03</b>
  * the definition, now in docs/explainer_multivar.md and
    the README: density is a share of the own grid
  * reduced-dimension variables get far fewer sites; the
    minimum-density check still applies to var0 only
  * requested_density for one variable, and rounding
    reading "differs" in every run
  * coverage: one row, var0, the variable the LHS stage
    covers; a "differs" there is a placement bug
  <b>Verified</b>: output files unchanged by 15aaa8a and
  e059ed9; serial and parallel reports now list the same
  rows apart from "values in parquet"; 553 tests pass.
end legend

@enduml
